    "source": "Bad Eden Bulwark + Shadow Courier v1.0 (RFI-native rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Signature move. Once a scene, you choose which kind of inevitability you are.</em></p><p><strong>Anchor or Advance — 1/scene (recovers on Soma Break).</strong> As part of any action on your turn, declare a stance. The chosen stance lasts until the end of your next turn:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Anchor.</strong> You cannot be moved against your will by any effect short of a Heroic-DC (22) push from a creature of your size or larger. Forced movement, knockback, teleportation targeting you, banishment, and dimensional swap effects all fail.</p></li><li><p><strong>Advance.</strong> You cannot be prevented from reaching a destination you declare on the same action. Difficult terrain, conditions that halve speed, reaction strikes, and zone-of-control effects do not stop your movement toward that point. You may still take damage along the way.</p></li></ul><p>Doctrine features at L5+ extend or modify which stance you favor.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
